      <comment>Above approximately 2200 m there are 80 to 140 cm of snow, and even as much as 170 cm in some localities, especially above approximately 2600 m. &lt;br/> Several medium-sized dry avalanches have been released especially on very steep slopes. &lt;br/> As a consequence of the occasionally strong northwesterly wind, fresh snow drift accumulations formed on Sunday. The snowpack will become in some cases unstable. &lt;br/> Towards its base, the snowpack is moist, in particular below approximately 2300 m.</comment>
    </snowpackStructure>
